WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Senator,
welcome back to the show.

00:00:01.735 --> 00:00:02.268 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
How are you?

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:03.536 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's great
to be back with you, Seth.

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:06.072
You know, all things considered,
I'm well.

00:00:06.072 --> 00:00:08.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, when one in five
mothers in America

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:10.777 align:start size:94% position:6%
is describing her children
under the age of 12

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:13.313 line:92%
as being hungry, I'm great

00:00:13.313 --> 00:00:16.282 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I feel the same way
when you put it in perspective

00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:17.283 align:start size:94% position:6%
I will say
it's a little strange.

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:20.086
This is the second time
you have been on the show

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:21.821 line:92%
since we've left the studio.

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:23.056 align:start size:94% position:6%
Once, I talked to you
from my attic,

00:00:23.056 --> 00:00:25.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
and now I join you
from my in-laws' house.

00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:30.296
And I want to say, it seem
as though your colleagues

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:34.200
in the Capitol are getting
better about wearing masks

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-But do you still try

00:00:35.135 --> 00:00:39.072
to avoid them as much as
possible, given the opportunity?

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:41.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now that you have
a good reason to avoid them.

00:00:41.775 --> 00:00:47.947
-I will tell you that I am still
very vigilant about wearing --

00:00:47.947 --> 00:00:51.951
I'm now actually, I've started
to sometimes wear double masks

00:00:51.951 --> 00:00:52.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughs ]
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:55.922 size:84% position:42%
-Like, the medical one,
you know, the blue one,

00:00:55.922 --> 00:01:00.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then, you know, whatever
the cloth one is over.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:02.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, they're wearing --
since the President

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:05.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
started wearing a mask,
I've noticed many more peopl

00:01:05.165 --> 00:01:05.965 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
are wearing masks.

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:07.367 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, that's interesting,
isn't it?

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:10.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, you know, it's more sad
than interesting because,

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:13.406
you know, President -- no matter
who the president is,

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:16.242 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's a reminder that they ca
set a good example,

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:18.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's a shame
it took this long.

00:01:18.645 --> 00:01:21.081 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I think what everybody
was saying is,

00:01:21.081 --> 00:01:24.517
when the person who is in charge
does the right thing,

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:28.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's amazing how many people
will follow that lead.

00:01:28.288 --> 00:01:29.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
And you're exactly right.

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:31.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, that is the power
of leadership, right?

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:37.297 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it is -- it is incumbent
on a person who has been

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:38.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
elected a leader
to actually understand

00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:40.567 align:start size:94% position:6%
the responsibilities
of leadership.

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:44.270 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, of course, Donald Trump
does not understand

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:46.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
the responsibilities
of leadership.

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:49.175
A real leader understands
that their strength is in

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:52.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
how they lift people up and no
how they beat people down,

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:55.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that is something
Donald Trump has never seeme

00:01:55.615 --> 00:01:58.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
to understand
since he took office.

00:01:58.818 --> 00:02:02.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
So that's why
I'm supporting Joe Biden.

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:05.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Someone who I would imagine
you believed

00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:09.629
did understand leadership wa
your colleague John Lewis.

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:11.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know he's lying in state now
in the Capitol.

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:14.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
Can you speak about
the example he set

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:18.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
and your history with him?
-Yeah.

00:02:18.004 --> 00:02:22.609 align:start size:94% position:6%
I remember having
many conversations with him,

00:02:22.609 --> 00:02:24.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
but one in particular,
in his office,

00:02:24.077 --> 00:02:25.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
which was like
a Civil Rights museum,

00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:30.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
because he has just lived
a full life of service, right?

00:02:30.216 --> 00:02:33.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
And from the time that he wa
a student and a young man

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:37.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
through just,
you know, days ago.

00:02:37.857 --> 00:02:42.829 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he was an American hero,
to be sure,

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:46.032 align:start size:94% position:6%
but one of the kindest peopl
that you could meet.

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:49.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, Seth, you know,
the type of person

00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:52.172 size:84% position:42%
who understands, again,
that there's strength,

00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:52.805 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
that their power --

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:55.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because he was
a very powerful man.

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:59.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it wasn't that he
demanded or carried power.

00:02:59.646 --> 00:03:02.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
He just was power.
He had powerful words.

00:03:02.715 --> 00:03:08.555
He had a power that was born
out of a love of our country

00:03:08.555 --> 00:03:12.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
a kindness,
and that gave him power,

00:03:12.725 --> 00:03:13.993 line:92%
and I'm gonna miss him so.

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:15.929
And, you know, one of the things
that I don't think has come ou

00:03:15.929 --> 00:03:20.466
as much about him, but I want to
make a point of mentioning it,

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:23.903 align:start size:94% position:6%
he was very encouraging
of women,

00:03:23.903 --> 00:03:28.208 align:start size:94% position:6%
and women in the professions
and women in leadership.

00:03:28.208 --> 00:03:31.144
And so, you can, you know,
the stories of Diane Nash

00:03:31.144 --> 00:03:34.614 align:start size:94% position:6%
or even the stories
that he would tell

00:03:34.614 --> 00:03:37.617 align:start size:94% position:6%
about the other women
of the movement

00:03:37.617 --> 00:03:40.320 align:start size:94% position:6%
that inspired him,
including Rosa Parks,

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:44.157
was one of the first people in
the movement who inspired him.

00:03:44.157 --> 00:03:46.559 line:92%
And I'm gonna miss him greatly

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:50.797
And I guess in a short way
of saying it, it's this.

00:03:50.797 --> 00:03:52.799 line:92%
John Lewis was about not onl

00:03:52.799 --> 00:03:55.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
walking across
the Edmund Pettus Bridge

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:57.303 line:92%
for the sake of voting right

00:03:57.303 --> 00:04:00.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the fight
for equality in America.

00:04:00.006 --> 00:04:01.441 line:92%
He was about building bridges.

00:04:01.441 --> 00:04:03.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
he wasn't about building walls

00:04:03.176 --> 00:04:04.010 line:92%
He was about building bridges.

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:06.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
He understood
the connection between people,

00:04:06.546 --> 00:04:07.313 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and he was a connecter.

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:10.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
He connected the fight
from the Civil Rights movement

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:13.052 size:84% position:42%
in the '50s and '60s
to what he did standing

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:16.689
in the front of the line,
talking about what we need to do

00:04:16.689 --> 00:04:19.959 align:start size:94% position:6%
around immigrants' rights,
that it's a civil-rights issue

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:24.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was a huge advocate
and fighter for LGBTQ rights

00:04:24.597 --> 00:04:26.299 size:81% position:41% line:92%
and marriage equality.

00:04:26.299 --> 00:04:30.603
He transcended all of these eras
and periods of time

00:04:30.603 --> 00:04:34.073 size:84% position:42%
but always consistently
fighting for equality

00:04:34.073 --> 00:04:35.942 line:92%
and dignity for all people

00:04:35.942 --> 00:04:39.879
-I know that you are now, as w
speak of dignity for all people,

00:04:39.879 --> 00:04:43.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
oftentimes that is the cas
of having the money

00:04:43.116 --> 00:04:45.652 size:84% position:42%
to support your family,
put food on the table.

00:04:45.652 --> 00:04:48.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were debating the $600
that's about to expire.

00:04:48.554 --> 00:04:52.792
-Can you speak to why
that number is both economically

00:04:52.792 --> 00:04:53.593 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and morally sound?

00:04:53.593 --> 00:04:56.062 size:84% position:42%
And also, can you speak
to the argument that,

00:04:56.062 --> 00:04:59.999
by giving Americans money,
we are disincentivizing them

00:04:59.999 --> 00:05:02.969
to return to a workforce,
even though those jobs,

00:05:02.969 --> 00:05:05.104 line:92%
in most cases, aren't there?

00:05:05.104 --> 00:05:09.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, we have had
over 40 million people,

00:05:09.175 --> 00:05:11.077 size:84% position:42%
at one time or another
in the last few months,

00:05:11.077 --> 00:05:13.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
lose their jobs.
Currently, we have a numbe

00:05:13.746 --> 00:05:16.182
of about 17 million people
are currently unemployed.

00:05:16.182 --> 00:05:20.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
Interestingly enough,
50% of African-American worker

00:05:20.586 --> 00:05:24.090 align:start size:94% position:6%
are now unemployed
since the pandemic.

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:29.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
In June, Seth, 1/3 of American
were not able to pay

00:05:29.095 --> 00:05:31.864 align:start size:94% position:6%
their housing costs,
rent or mortgage.

00:05:31.864 --> 00:05:33.700 size:75% position:38%
One in five mothers,
like I said earlier,

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:37.470
is describing her children under
the age of 12 as being hungry.

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:40.673 align:start size:94% position:6%
People are hurting in America,
hurting deeply.

00:05:40.673 --> 00:05:44.911
And so what I am proposing
is that during the course

00:05:44.911 --> 00:05:48.381 align:start size:94% position:6%
of this pandemic, until we hav
seen our way out of it,

00:05:48.381 --> 00:05:51.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
there should be a moratorium
on evictions,

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:53.953 line:92%
a moratorium on foreclosures

00:05:53.953 --> 00:05:55.588 align:start size:94% position:6%
that there should be
a moratorium --

00:05:55.588 --> 00:05:57.757 align:start size:94% position:6%
which means, basically,
a pause --

00:05:57.757 --> 00:05:59.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
on turning off
people's utilities,

00:05:59.859 --> 00:06:01.928 line:92%
including their water service.

00:06:01.928 --> 00:06:04.731
'Cause, by the way, people
can't pay their water bill

00:06:04.731 --> 00:06:08.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
when they are not working,
and you need to wash your hand

00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:10.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
to protect your family
from the virus.

00:06:10.670 --> 00:06:13.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
So that's what my
R.E.L.I.E.F. Act calls for

00:06:13.072 --> 00:06:16.476 align:start size:94% position:6%
just to give people relief
and let them just --

00:06:16.476 --> 00:06:20.079
to the extent that we can,
survive through the course

00:06:20.079 --> 00:06:22.982 align:start size:94% position:6%
of this pandemic so that,
at the end of it,

00:06:22.982 --> 00:06:24.117 line:92%
they can get back on their feet.

00:06:24.117 --> 00:06:26.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
We don't want people
to fall further

00:06:26.486 --> 00:06:28.121 line:92%
and further through the cracks

00:06:28.121 --> 00:06:30.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because at some point,
we need to recover.

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:32.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so let's see people
and carry them

00:06:32.392 --> 00:06:36.596
through these days and these
months to get on the other sid

00:06:36.596 --> 00:06:38.197 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and with dignity.

00:06:38.197 --> 00:06:40.133 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I do --
Because obviously this is

00:06:40.133 --> 00:06:42.235 size:75% position:38%
a very serious topic
we're talking about,

00:06:42.235 --> 00:06:45.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
but on a lighter side,
I do want to compliment --

00:06:45.872 --> 00:06:48.241 align:start size:94% position:6%
The R.E.L.I.E.F. Act
is an acronym.

00:06:48.241 --> 00:06:49.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want to make sure
I get this right.

00:06:49.275 --> 00:06:53.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
Rent Emergencies Leave Impacts
on Evicted Families Act.

00:06:53.913 --> 00:06:56.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
Who comes up with
these acronyms, Senator?

00:06:56.215 --> 00:06:58.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
There's, like, a whole group

00:06:58.651 --> 00:07:01.220 align:start size:94% position:6%
of people
who work on those things.

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:04.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's really --
It's kind of part of

00:07:04.524 --> 00:07:07.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
the funny art
of the United States Congress.

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:10.463 size:84% position:42%
Like, there are people
who spend a lot of time

00:07:10.463 --> 00:07:14.534
coming up with these acronyms,
and they're often very good.

00:07:14.534 --> 00:07:17.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And, I mean, I guess the goal
of these acronyms is,

00:07:17.236 --> 00:07:20.673 align:start size:94% position:6%
you want to make it so that,
you know --

00:07:20.673 --> 00:07:22.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this is
either party would do this

00:07:22.909 --> 00:07:24.877 align:start size:94% position:6%
You try to name it something
that you would

00:07:24.877 --> 00:07:26.746 size:78% position:39%
shame your colleagues
into voting against,

00:07:26.746 --> 00:07:28.181 align:start size:94% position:6%
something like
the R.E.L.I.E.F. Act

00:07:28.181 --> 00:07:30.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
or the C.A.R.E.S. Act or -
I mean, it seems to me

00:07:30.683 --> 00:07:33.186 align:start size:94% position:6%
like you should try to make --
-The H.E.R.O.E.S. Act.

00:07:33.186 --> 00:07:36.189 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The K.I.T.T.E.N. Act.
Just anything.

00:07:36.189 --> 00:07:36.956 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
No, right.

00:07:36.956 --> 00:07:40.326
Like, I don't know that we hav
yet had the Santa Claus act,

00:07:40.326 --> 00:07:42.628 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I think you're raising
a fair point.

00:07:42.628 --> 00:07:45.998
-Yeah.
-I think -- but it is also about

00:07:45.998 --> 00:07:47.800 align:start size:94% position:6%
speaking to the values
that are at play

00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:50.570
in the legislation and certainly
with the R.E.L.I.E.F. Act,

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:53.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
it is --
that is a very important value

00:07:53.773 --> 00:07:56.909
-Yes, that is a fair one.
The acronym does line up

00:07:56.909 --> 00:07:58.778 align:start size:94% position:6%
with the core principles
behind the act.

00:07:58.778 --> 00:08:00.847 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
Yeah.

